# A record whose head is an ordinary Structure launches it in code separated from its data (the author 2026-11-11,
# LMX_blog/2026-11-11.md#structure-call-by-name; R21, R22; plan M11 5b): in a callable's code `Own()` runs Own over
# itself, `Bump(Counter)` and `Bump(data := Counter)` run Bump over the data Counter -- the one argument data, given by
# position or by name.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the call
# main(). The dump of the root prints main as written, so the places own_n and counter_n hold what the dump of Own and
# Counter showed.
sub: main () (
    Own: (int: n 5; n := n + 1)
    Bump: (n := n + 1)
    Counter: (int: n 0)
    int: seen 0
)
    fn: f () int
        Own()
        Own()
        Bump(Counter)
        Bump(data := Counter)
        return: Own\n * 10 + Counter\n
    seen := f()
main()
int: seen main\data\seen
int: own_n main\data\Own\n
int: counter_n main\data\Counter\n
